    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nSince [this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/commit/0c5f49e349539aebba7384a2ede7b22ecffbaa7e) commit, the cursor disappears when switching from file a to file b using mini.pick.\r\n\r\nI tested with an [older](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/commit/49e2699dc0d585b445eda24ed4bb45952ac20508) commit, and the cursor does not disappear.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen neovim and open a file. Cursor is visible.\r\nNow, use pick.files to open another file. Cursor disappears.\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCursor does not disappear...;)\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nCursor disappears",
