        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Regarding the Neovim issue: I think it was [this](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/21480#issuecomment-1360746259) one.\r\n\r\nI *think* this was a suggestion to use `set guicursor=` inside autocommand for `VimLeave`. The cursor links to a [FAQ entry](https://neovim.io/doc/user/faq.html#faq-general) which in fact suggests `au VimLeave,VimSuspend * set guicursor=a:block-blinkon0`.\r\n\r\n**Edit**: yeah, it does seem like a [suggestion for `VimLeave`](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/4396#issuecomment-1377191592).",
            "created_at": "2024-08-16T19:43:18Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1149#issuecomment-2294108456",
            "id": 2294108456,
